SAFE_KEY = /^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_-]*$/ — this regex ALLOWS hyphens! So `Content-Type` matches SAFE_KEY (because `[A-Za-z0-9_-]*` includes '-'), so it's emitted unquoted. That's the bug: SAFE_KEY permits hyphens, so header names with '-' are treated as safe JS identifiers. This is a genuine bug. Line 229 defines SAFE_KEY.

